  "status": "verified-sample",
  "coverage": "complete",
  "notes": [
    "Complete list: 5 actions (src/actions.ts) and 2 boolean feedbacks (src/feedbacks.ts). The module talks OSC to ONYX (the \"Mx\" address space, e.g. /Mx/button/<n>, /Mx/fader/<n>). Bitfocus also lists the telnet-based module obsidiancontrol-onyx, catalogued separately with a different action set.",
    "The button dropdowns of generic_button (123 names) and generic_button_led (94 names with LED or text feedback) are built from the closed table in src/buttons.ts at startup (getButtonActionChoices, getButtonLedFeedbackChoices); the catalog lists them in source order. The OSC address of each button is not catalogued.",
    "The playback numbers (1-20) map to OSC base addresses through getPlaybackBaseAddressNum (src/index.ts); the \"Down\" button (id 4) is offered by the playback feedback but, according to the label and a source comment, never provides feedback.",
    "playback_level_relative reads the current level from the variable playback_NN_level at run time; without a known level it starts from 0.",
    "The module has no expression support: it is built on @companion-module/base ~1.4.3.",
    "Variables and presets are not catalogued."
  ],
